A||||1||wkayl||WOW...what a drive!!!||||1||
Z||000000||wkayl||05-21-2000||02:54 AM||||I put about 150 miles on my 86 GT today.  About 100 of them in the Rocky Mountains.  On one of the drives fron Loveland Co west to Estes Park, I drove on a winding canyon road with a 40mph speed limit (I know this for a fact because a few months ago a nice officer wrote me note saying so).  I set the cruise at 45mph and drove 25 miles without touching the brakes.  I had to put a little muscle into the steering wheel a few times. There was a small red car following me that would hang close on the straight sections, but faded when the curves came up.  I was about 1 mile from the end of the drive when I came up behind a tourist going 40.  Dang I wanted to make it all the way, but I was smiling anyhow.  It made me think of those guys that drive a closed course and can push it to the limits.  I wish I didn't have to work for a living and could just drive and smile.||||reg||1
Z||000001||Coconut||05-21-2000||08:27 PM||||waykl, yeah I just live for those nice tight curves. Man, it gives me a hard on just thinking about long windy roads, ain't nuthin' more fun than taking a drive in our fieros and doing the cruise. Glad you had fun! As soon as I can get some time, I'm filling the tank, grabbing the old lady,and taking off for destinations unknown! Just as long as I can do it in my little Pontiac, thats all I'll ever need!!!<P>                    Keep on Cruisin'<BR>                     Coconut||||reg||14
